# The record format is LF (docs/normalized-record-schema.md). A CRLF checkout
# made every normalized record unreadable, and the failure looked like missing
# frontmatter rather than like line endings.
* text=auto eol=lf

# The Enron fixtures are invented messages in an export's wire format, CRLF
# included - tests/test_enron_fixtures.py asserts it, because the converter
# (#78) has to strip it. Normalizing them to LF would erase the property they
# exist to hold. `-text` turns every conversion off for these files.
tests/fixtures/enron/*.eml -text
